From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thongass000 <tienthong2004@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:54:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] EpdgService: Report the tunnel IPv4 address as /32

Samsung's ePDG gives the tunnel's IPv4 address a prefix length of 0.
Tethering's PrivateAddressCoordinator then sees 0.0.0.0/0 in use and
finds no free IPv4 prefix, so hotspot and USB tethering failed while
Wi-Fi Calling was up. Report a prefix length of 0 as 32.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../com/sec/epdg/EpdgRilInterface$IWlanLinkProperties.smali  | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali/com/sec/epdg/EpdgRilInterface$IWlanLinkProperties.smali b/smali/com/sec/epdg/EpdgRilInterface$IWlanLinkProperties.smali
index 44dc1fd..0850751 100644
--- a/smali/com/sec/epdg/EpdgRilInterface$IWlanLinkProperties.smali
+++ b/smali/com/sec/epdg/EpdgRilInterface$IWlanLinkProperties.smali
@@ -306,6 +306,11 @@
     .line 229
     iget v0, p0, Lcom/sec/epdg/EpdgRilInterface$IWlanLinkProperties;->mIpv4PrefixLen:I
 
+    if-nez v0, :cond_0
+
+    const/16 v0, 0x20
+
+    :cond_0
     return v0
 .end method
 
